    "notes": "Anything Labs is a public project brand, not a verified legal issuer entity in the reviewed disclosures. Payment and settlement marketing is evident, but the website, access page, issuance page and whitepaper do not establish a fixed monetary-value redemption obligation. Applicability therefore remains unclear rather than asserting a payment-stablecoin classification. No legal entity, domicile, licensing regulator or GENIUS issuer route is inferred. The complete OCC pending-applicant table was recovered from raw official HTML and contains no Anything Labs entry. The Federal Register exact-name search returned zero documents through October 7, 2026; opened framework sources, NYDFS tables and bounded regulator-domain searches did not identify a qualifying token-specific approval, official application, foreign registration or enforcement action. No reserve composition/report, fixed-value redemption policy or monthly attestation was located in the reviewed issuer corpus. Rulemaking remains pre-effective; not-yet-restricted does not assert affirmative legal availability. This is an editorial scope assessment and a bounded public-source negative finding, not a regulator ruling or proof that unpublished filings do not exist.",
